# P1-INT-00 owns this file. It is the environment contract for the P01 PostgreSQL/S3
# foundation: every name frozen by FF-01 section 3 appears here exactly once.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is git-ignored and is never committed. The values below are DISPOSABLE LOCAL
# EXAMPLES for a throwaway container pair. They are not secrets, they are not used by
# any deployed system, and they must not be reused anywhere real.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LANE ISOLATION - read before `make up`.
# FF-01 section 5 forbids two authoring lanes from sharing live service state. Before
# starting services, give YOUR lane its own values for all six of:
#
#   FOUNDATION_INSTANCE  POSTGRES_PORT  S3_API_PORT  S3_CONSOLE_PORT
#   POSTGRES_DB          S3_BUCKET
#
# The compose project name, network and volume names all derive from
# FOUNDATION_INSTANCE, so changing it gives the lane its own volumes. A lane may not
# run `make up` against another lane's instance. Suggested convention:
#
#   lane        INSTANCE                    PG_PORT  S3_API  S3_CONSOLE  POSTGRES_DB                S3_BUCKET
#   P1-INF-01   auditmanager-p1-inf-01      55432    59000   59001       auditmanager_p1_inf_01     auditmanager-p1-inf-01
#   P1-DB-01    auditmanager-p1-db-01       55433    59010   59011       auditmanager_p1_db_01      auditmanager-p1-db-01
#   P1-STO-01   auditmanager-p1-sto-01      55434    59020   59021       auditmanager_p1_sto_01     auditmanager-p1-sto-01
#   P1-QA-00    auditmanager-p1-qa-00       55435    59030   59031       auditmanager_p1_qa_00      auditmanager-p1-qa-00
#
# All six values change per lane, not just the first three.
#
# SHELL SYNTAX. `make` loads this file by sourcing it, so each line must be valid shell:
# quote any value containing a space or a shell metacharacter, e.g.
#   POSTGRES_PASSWORD='p@ss word'
# and percent-encode it inside DATABASE_URL as described below.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# COHERENCE. POSTGRES_* and MINIO_ROOT_* configure the disposable local services;
# DATABASE_URL and S3_* are the application-facing values. The two sides must agree,
# and `make` verifies that they do before touching any service: DATABASE_URL must
# carry the same user, password, port and database as the POSTGRES_* names, and
# S3_ENDPOINT_URL must carry S3_API_PORT. If a password contains characters that are
# special in a URL, percent-encode it inside DATABASE_URL only.
#
# Container image identity is NOT configured here. Postgres, MinIO and mc are pinned by
# tag and digest in the Makefile and docs/program/FOUNDATION_LOCK.json, and the Makefile
# exports them to compose as FOUNDATION_POSTGRES_IMAGE, FOUNDATION_S3_IMAGE and
# FOUNDATION_S3_MC_IMAGE. Do not set those here and do not pin an image anywhere else.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- lane identity ---
# Names the disposable local instance. Compose project, network and volumes derive
# from it. One value per lane, never shared.
FOUNDATION_INSTANCE=auditmanager-foundation-local

# --- disposable local PostgreSQL service ---
POSTGRES_DB=auditmanager_foundation_local
POSTGRES_USER=auditmanager_local
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=local-disposable-postgres-password
POSTGRES_PORT=55432

# --- application-facing database value ---
# Driver is fixed by the lock: psycopg 3 through SQLAlchemy, hence postgresql+psycopg.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://auditmanager_local:local-disposable-postgres-password@127.0.0.1:55432/auditmanager_foundation_local

# --- disposable local S3-compatible (MinIO) service ---
# MinIO refuses a root password shorter than 8 characters.
MINIO_ROOT_USER=local-disposable-minio-root
MINIO_ROOT_PASSWORD=local-disposable-minio-password

# --- application-facing object storage values ---
# Locally the application authenticates with the same disposable root credentials as
# the container. This is a throwaway local convenience, NOT an IAM design: scoped
# service credentials, multiple buckets and any production account layout are
# explicitly out of scope for FF-01 (section 4) and belong to a later task.
S3_ENDPOINT_URL=http://127.0.0.1:59000
S3_API_PORT=59000
S3_CONSOLE_PORT=59001
S3_REGION=us-east-1
S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=local-disposable-minio-root
S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=local-disposable-minio-password
S3_BUCKET=auditmanager-foundation-local
